<a id="interior-lower-statue-workshop-and-upper-bedchamber"></a>

### Arc Three — A labor prison and a collapsing stronghold

Eight black obelisks and green flames mark the pyramid's approaches. Guards carrying psychic spears oversee ragged elves who clear sand and haul stone and treasure from stripped tombs. The place combines a seat of power with a labor camp, its enslaved inhabitants serving work they cannot freely leave.[^outside]

Inside, a lower hall has become a workshop. Scaffolding surrounds an enormous unfinished statue bearing Khalazar's screaming face; tubes feed black ichor into it, and parts from a dismantled mechanical spider supply its construction. An upper bedchamber contains a canopy bed, an ichor fountain and the desiccated body of the ruler. Adjacent rooms hold underfed workers, raw butchered creatures and crude equipment filtering grey water from the dark supply.[^interior]

The guild expedition turns the stronghold's hard floors into escape routes. Evelyn destroys the skeletal bat guarding the balcony while the others prepare the rescue. Koh and Dominic subdue captive workers without killing them, and allies carry people to Darmah's first teleportation circle. Wildfire, Withers and others are taken to the Guild. As the search moves upstairs, Evelyn cuts the statue's feeding tubes, interrupting its supply without yet bringing it down. Hissia and Keeves are found and brought down for the remaining rescue.[^rescue]

In the upper chamber, the Delvers restore the organs from their three urns to Khalazar's body. A shared revelation and an apparently restored ancient city draw them into a final confrontation. The bright, inhabited city proves illusory: the real bedchamber remains beneath it. Together the three drive Koh's spectral dagger into Khalazar's heart, destroying him.[^defeat]

The physical pyramid collapses. Its unfinished statue is crushed with the surrounding masonry, while Chad Brad and Corgan shield the escaping party from falling stone. Darmah's second circle carries the remaining rescuers and captives back to the Guild. The stronghold that sustained forced labor becomes a ruin.[^collapse]

## Current status

The pyramid is ruined and Khalazar defeated. Surviving captives and expedition members have escaped, though the exact rescued total is uncertain. The wider desert's later condition, the mined crystal's remaining uses and the fate of unvisited ruins are unknown.[^status]

[^desert]: [S3E11](../../episodes/S3E11.md), ~00:00–00:30. [Triangle gate](triangle-gate-catacombs.md) actually opens, expedition enters and door closes behind it. Vast cavern ceiling is unseen, not a surveyed height. Crystal resemblance to earlier dream light and golem cores is interpreted; visibly mined/cut portion has no proved user or purpose. Koh takes a roughly three-inch shard. Free Action supports his no-footprint sand travel by played ruling; elk likewise crosses readily. Hidden roper is noticed and avoided, not fought. Original map/audio not examined.
[^outside]: [S3E11](../../episodes/S3E11.md), ~00:30–01:20. Eight obelisks, stripped tombs, mummy-like spear guards and compelled labor are observed. Guard deaths are separate from stable nonlethal worker knockouts. Eleven outside is one observed subtotal, not a final colony census. [Skeletal bat](../creatures/skeletal-bat-balcony.md) appearance and later defeat remain separate from the workers' condition.
[^interior]: [S3E11](../../episodes/S3E11.md), ~01:20–02:05, lower workshop and upper bedchamber; [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md), ~00:35–01:00, side rooms with six and eight captives, butchered hook horror/grick food and seep filter. Statue around ninety feet and balcony around three hundred feet are spoken estimates, not surveyed architecture. Grey water's appearance does not prove potable safety or contagion. First view does not positively identify Hissia or activate the body; the later visit does. Darmah's Spider Climb enables Koh's actual infiltration rather than a flight or invented doorway.
[^rescue]: [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md), ~00:00–01:00. Bat destroyed by Evelyn's radiant weapon; same elk is resummoned after banishment. First completed circle returns workers including Buck Wildfire, Alexandre Withers and Phelan, with eight minotaurs and Boonfellow; Chad Brad/Corgan remain. Discussed Remove Curse is retracted, not cast on captives. Hissia/Keeves are positively identified and subdued alive; Nopa and Corgan carry them. Tubes are severed before the statue's later destruction. Conflicting planning numbers do not yield a confirmed total rescue count. [Finale comparison](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E12_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md).
[^defeat]: [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md), ~01:00–02:40. [Three urn organs](../items/three-urns-triangle-gate.md) are physically inserted in the body's back. Shaolin's extra ancestral-blood drop is not explicitly applied. Historical vision and restored-city battle are magical/psychic, not independent documentary history or a physically rebuilt city. Final joint heart thrust and disintegration happen in the real chamber, not merely defeat of another shade. The core trio survive, despite real unconsciousness and death-save danger during the fight.
[^collapse]: [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md), ~02:14–02:43. Real pyramid collapse destroys the statue; Darmah's second circle actually evacuates the remaining group to Guild basement. Exact medical recovery of Darmah before escape is not separately narrated. [November creator retrospective](../../../episodes/BONUS-2021-11-13.md), ~41:30–50:30, describes a possible giant iron-golem boss, back-mounted sarcophagus, eye lasers, Atomer attack and flying-pyramid empire. These are unused branches, not missed played events. Statue never animates; cutting tubes alone does not smash it. No all-captive medical or headcount audit is inferred.
[^status]: [S3E12](../../episodes/S3E12.md) supplies the real defeat, evacuation and later waning monsters/renewed land, with no further physical visit here. The pyramid's destruction is not a claim every desert ruin, adjoining catacomb or distant spa is destroyed. Curse-lifted minotaurs become inert bones at the Guild, not resurrected laborers here. [S3E11 comparison](../../../reports/DELVERS_S3E11_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md) and [creator comparison](../../../reports/BONUS_2021_11_13_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-26.md) remain provenance, not fresh audio review.
